---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../data/site';
---
<SiteLayout title="Layout" description="Explore three ways to organise the Immortals Macau flagship: Club, Gallery and Salon, with private suites and dedicated assessment rooms." active="layout">
<section class="wrap page-heading"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href={url()}>Macau flagship</a><span>/</span><span>Layout</span></div><p class="eyebrow">01 / THE SPATIAL PLAN</p><div class="page-heading-grid"><h1>One footprint.<br /><span>Three possibilities.</span></h1><div><p>Curved glazing, generous daylight and a double-height arrival. A former private casino, reimagined around a different kind of visit.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="#plans">Explore the three plans <span>↓</span></a></div></div></div><div class="facts-row"><div><strong>1,100 <small>m²</small></strong><p>Reported total footprint</p></div><div><strong>04</strong><p>Window-facing private suites</p></div><div><strong>03</strong><p>Dedicated assessment rooms</p></div><div><strong>2.4 <small>m</small></strong><p>Main corridor clear-width target</p></div></div></section>
<section class="cream" id="plans"><div class="wrap section"><div class="chapter-line"><span>THE PUBLIC FLOOR</span><span>THREE OPTIONS / NO PREFERRED LAYOUT</span></div><div class="section-heading"><h2>Where should<br />the visit begin?</h2><p>The private clinical framework stays consistent. The public floor changes its emphasis: a lounge-led welcome, an open gallery or a larger flexible salon.</p></div><div class="layout-stage"><div class="layout-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Choose a layout"><button data-layout="0" class="active" aria-pressed="true"><span>01</span> Club <small>A lounge-led welcome</small></button><button data-layout="1" aria-pressed="false"><span>02</span> Gallery <small>An open discovery floor</small></button><button data-layout="2" aria-pressed="false"><span>03</span> Salon <small>A flexible hosted space</small></button></div><div class="layout-body"><div class="plan-display"><button id="open-plan" aria-label="Enlarge the Club floor plan"><img id="plan-image" src={url('assets/plan-club.svg')} alt="Club layout: four window suites, separate assessments and a lounge-led public floor" /><span class="enlarge-label">Explore the full plan <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></button></div><div class="layout-notes" aria-live="polite"><p class="eyebrow" id="plan-number">LAYOUT 01</p><h3 id="plan-title">A lounge-led welcome</h3><p id="plan-description">Arrival opens into a generous lounge. A defined threshold leads into the gallery, with space for conversation, discovery and hosted sessions.</p><div id="allocation" class="allocation"></div><p class="tradeoff" id="plan-tradeoff">The largest dedicated lounge of the three options, with a mid-sized gallery and flexible salon.</p><p class="footnote">Indicative public-space areas, calibrated to the reported footprint. These are concept layouts, not surveyed architectural drawings.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap section"><div class="chapter-line"><span>THE CONSTANTS</span><span>A PUBLIC INVITATION / A PRIVATE CLINICAL WORLD</span></div><div class="section-heading"><h2>Two ways in.<br />One considered visit.</h2><p>The main entrance welcomes guests into the public experience. A separate patient arrival supports a quieter route into the private clinic.</p></div><div class="plan-summary-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">01 / PUBLIC DISCOVERY</p><h3>Room for curiosity.</h3><p>The gallery, lounge, coffee bar and flexible salon create different settings for a first encounter. Experience placement follows the chosen layout and each activity’s practical requirements.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">02 / PERSONAL CARE</p><h3>A suite as your base.</h3><p>Four permanent, window-facing suites provide a private setting for the visit, with showers and room for conversation. Dedicated assessment rooms support specific tests and equipment.</p></article><article><p class="eyebrow">03 / EVERYDAY OPERATION</p><h3>The work behind the welcome.</h3><p>Clinical support, a separate patient entry, circulation and fire escape provision remain part of the planning framework. Final routes, clearances and equipment requirements need detailed coordination.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="cream"><div class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>The plan is the framework.<br />Design gives it feeling.</h2><p>The four interior directions explore atmosphere within the same clinic brief. Room images are design studies and should be coordinated against the selected plan.</p></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={url('interior-design/')}>Compare the interior directions <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={url('experiences/')}>Discover the experiences <span>↗</span></a></div></div></section>
<dialog id="plan-dialog" aria-labelledby="plan-dialog-title"><div class="dialog-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">SPATIAL CONCEPT / FULL DRAWING</p><h2 id="plan-dialog-title">Club layout</h2></div><button id="close-plan">Close ×</button></div><div class="plan-toolbar"><div class="plan-modal-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Floor plan"><button data-modal-plan="0">Club</button><button data-modal-plan="1">Gallery</button><button data-modal-plan="2">Salon</button></div><div class="zoom-controls"><button id="zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button><span id="zoom-level">100%</span><button id="zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom in">+</button><button id="zoom-reset">Fit</button></div></div><div class="plan-viewport" tabindex="0" aria-label="Floor plan, scroll to explore when zoomed"><img id="large-plan" src={url('assets/plan-club.svg')} alt="Club floor plan" /></div></dialog>
<script>import '../scripts/layout-explorer.js';</script>
</SiteLayout>
